# Embedded IoT Homework 2 - PWM & OLED Monitoring
**Name:** Khudaira Babar  
**Reg No:** 24-NTU-CS-FL-1041  

## Overview
This project implements hardware PWM using the ESP32 to fade two LEDs at different frequencies. Live monitoring of the configured frequencies and dynamic duty cycles is output to an SSD1306 OLED display via I2C.

## Hardware Wiring
* **LED 1 (Red):** Connected to GPIO 16 via a 330-ohm current-limiting resistor. 
* **LED 2 (Green):** Connected to GPIO 17 via a 330-ohm current-limiting resistor.
* **SSD1306 OLED:** Connected to I2C pins SDA (GPIO 21) and SCL (GPIO 22). Powered via 3.3V.

## PWM Configuration & Duty Cycle Control
* **LED 1 Frequency:** 5000 Hz 
* **LED 2 Frequency:** 1000 Hz 
* **Resolution:** 8-bit (values 0 - 255)
* **Duty Cycle:** A `for` loop dynamically increments and decrements the duty cycle from 0 to 255 and back to 0. 

## OLED Output & Test Results
The OLED correctly displays the static configured frequencies for both LEDs alongside the live percentage of the current duty cycle, updating dynamically as the LEDs fade in and out. The circuit was successfully verified in Wokwi simulation and on physical ESP32 hardware.